From eb19e8aba790202a5b78642aa4bbf13aef5db5bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-perf <perf@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:46:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] x86: per-path flag liveness in the flag-consumer walk

The walk stopped at ANY writer, so a PARTIAL writer such as stc (CF only)
or sahf (all but OF) hid every consumer standing behind it.  eliminate_redundant_
self_test deletes test %R,%R based on flag_consumers_are_zf_only, so a jo
behind an stc read the PRODUCER's OF without the walk ever seeing it and the
fold fired:

    addl $1, %eax        ; x = 0x7fffffff -> OF = 1
    testl %eax, %eax     ; deleted, and it would clear OF
    je .Lzero            ; ZF-only consumer, not taken
    stc                  ; CF only -- the coarse walk stopped HERE
    jo .Lof              ; reads the producer's OF; must veto

Executed as an A/B this returns 1 originally and 0 folded: a wrong answer
from code that lowers the instruction count, assembles, links, and passes
every shape-only gate.

Fix: thread a per-path LIVE mask through the worklist and intersect it with
cc_reads(cc) and !preserved at each consumer.  A writer only KILLS the flags
it defines; it no longer ends the walk, because what it does not define is
still live from the producer.  cmc is special-cased: it COMPLEMENTS CF
rather than defining it, so CF stays live and a jb behind it still vetoes.

This is strictly more information than the old static 'preserved' compare
and also strictly more precise, never merely more conservative: a full
writer kills everything and the walk still stops, and a consumer of a flag
an earlier writer retired is charged nothing, so the folds the coarse rule
kept are still kept.

Side effect: flags_reach_a_whole_flags_reader (preserved = 0) becomes
strictly dominated by flags_reach_a_whole_flags_reader_except_af and loses
its last production caller, so it is removed rather than left as a trap.

The two callers now pass the preserved set they actually prove: F_ZF for
flag_consumers_are_zf_only (ZF is identical across the and/or/xor, same-width
arithmetic and zero-extending width-change classes) and F_ZF|F_CF for
flag_consumers_are_zf_cf_only, which already documented exactly that.

